maria: Quick heads-up — found a couple of docs snippets still using the old `client.stream(...)` pattern in the SDK examples for py/ts/go. I'll open a PR with suggested replacements.
lee: Where exactly? point me to the pages and i'll take TS/Go.
sasha: I can pick up Go too. which pages are broken?
maria: Two places: `/docs/sdk/streaming.md` and `/docs/examples/pagination.md`. The streaming page has synchronous `for chunk in client.stream(...)` examples that confuse folks now that we encourage the async iterator / event-driven pattern. Example problematic snippet:```py
for chunk in client.stream(model="x", prompt=prompt):
    if chunk.err:
        retry()
    process(chunk)
```
We should replace with a concise async example + mention backoff/retry guidelines.
rahul: I'll own Python. plan: convert to `async for` example and add a small helper showing exponential backoff with jitter.
lee: For TS i'll change from `client.stream(...)` callback style to `for await (const chunk of client.stream(...)) {}` and add a `retryWithBackoff` util. quick sketch:```ts
async function retryWithBackoff(fn){
  for (let i=0;i<5;i++){
    try { return await fn() }
    catch(e){ await new Promise(r=>setTimeout(r, Math.pow(2,i)*100 + Math.random()*100)) }
  }
  throw new Error('retry failed')
}
```
sasha: For Go i'll swap the old blocking example to the new channel-based pattern and add note about closing KV cache / draining before reconnect. small snippet:```go
ch := client.Stream(ctx, req)
for msg := range ch {
  if msg.Err != nil { // handle retry externally }
  handle(msg)
}
```
doc-bot: link-checker: Broken link detected in `/docs/examples/pagination.md` -> reference to `/docs/sdk/old-pagination` (404).
maria: Good catch. We'll update the pagination doc to use `cursor` examples that match the SDK param names (`cursor_id`, `page_size`) and remove the old link. Also add a migration note: "If you rely on resuming a session, persist `cursor_id` server-side and check TTL".
rahul: Adding a tiny pytest for the python snippet so docs CI validates sample runs: `pytest docs/tests/test_stream_snippet.py::test_async_iter_example`. I'll include fixtures to mock streaming responses.
lee: Branching plan: `docs/streaming-snippet-updates/{py,ts,go}`. I'll open the TS PR and assign @sasha and @maria as reviewers.
maria: I'll open the master PR bundling all three language updates (so one preview page) — PR #4876. Targeting merge by Friday EOD. No breaking changes to SDK, just docs.
sasha: LGTM :thumbsup:
doc-bot: ci-docs: preview build started for PR #4876.
deploy-bot: docs-preview: https://deployments.redwood.dev/preview/4876 available in ~4m.
maria: Thanks all — once previews look good i'll request final review and merge. If anyone sees other snippet mismatches please drop them here or tag me.
